0)#!kvd:=
1) asm-list-riscv64.fd -- RISC-V 64 instruction templates for
2)lib-asm-riscv64.fun. GENERATED by
2)  fun/lib/tools/gen-asm-list-riscv64.py <binutils-src>
2)from GNU binutils (verified against 2.44). Do not hand-edit; refresh
2)with the script and re-run fun/test/tools/asm-riscv64-diff.sh.
1)
1) key   = "<mnemonic> <op-shape>,..."   e.g. addi r,r,#
2)value = "<8 hex base>|<slot>..."      e.g. 01300000|r0@7|r1@15|y2@20:12
1)
1) Slots: r = GPR at bit; v = unsigned imm; y = signed imm; m = raw masked
2)value (low half of a split displacement). Optional ":w" is the field width
2)and ":s" scales the value by 2^s.
1)
1) A load/store key lists the memory operand as two entries ("r,#,r"), because
2)`ld a0, 8(sp)` expands to an offset and a base register.
1)
1) After editing, rebuild the packed form with:
2)  src/prj/fun/funcmd fun/lib/tools/make-asm-list.fun \
4)    fun/lib/asm-list-riscv64.fd
